## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_drips.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Drips generates a layered-noise pattern that imitates drips. It works as a mask or as a building block for more intricate textures, such as water marks on windows.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Drips produit un motif de gouttes par bruits superposés, utilisable en masque pour des traces d'eau sur une vitre.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Output range: Amplitude scales values, Center offsets them, Mask Contrast adjusts contrast first", "Pattern: Element Size, Offset, Tile Size as repeat period", "Density: number of foreground drops", "Distortion: horizontal waver of the drops", "Primary Trailing and Secondary Trailing: stretch drops downward into streaks", "Secondary Mask, Tertiary Mask, Speckle Mask: visibility of background drops, smudges and specks", "Seed: changes the randomization while keeping the same look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can be negative or above 1; use the Clamp options", "Complement works as intended only for values from 0 to 1", "Fold has no effect when all values are positive", "Post-processing Contrast is separate from Noise Contrast", "Tile Size should match the aspect ratio of non-square images", "Introduced in Houdini 22.0"]

